  "_notes": [
    "\uD83D\uDEA9 v1.8 (877 §2.6) — capabilities.capabilityReasons is a Record<string,string> keyed by CAPABILITY NAME, valued as a typed code the client words. Absent or {} where nothing is shut; fixture 01 records the empty case. The keys are camelCase on the wire because System.Text.Json's naming policy applies to properties only.",
    "The rule is DocumentSourcePolicyService's SupportsPickInStore — WSFD / P2E / DKSW are delivery-only — and the list lives server-side in DocumentSourceFulfilmentPolicy, which CC2's WPF service now delegates to. A client-side list of source codes was REJECTED: DocumentSourceCategory membership is table data, so a console holding the list is a second opinion that goes stale silently.",
    "It is the surviving half of a rule 175 stated too widely. 175 carried \"P2E forces online payment + the delivery-only sources\" as one item; 155 found the payment half sits on the KIND axis, where every forcing kind is out of phase 1. This half is a SOURCE rule, and phase 1 has sources.",
    "capabilityReasons.canChangePaymentType is UNREACHABLE in phase 1 by ruling (§2.4) and appears in no fixture. It is wired so that a forcing rule arriving later is a server DATA change, not a client change.",
    "\uD83D\uDEA9 Only the flip TO pickup is refused, and the CAPABILITY says exactly that. setFulfilment(Delivery) stays legal on every order, and an order ALREADY under pickup with a delivery-only source (reachable — setDocumentSource carries no fulfilment guard) keeps canChangeFulfilment TRUE with no reason: the one move left to it is the one that resolves the combination. A source rule must never be able to strand an order in a mode it cannot leave."
  ]
}
